# Everything the Makefile writes goes under $(BUILD): object files and their
# generated .d dependency lists, the vmlinux.h dumped from the running kernel,
# the BPF skeleton, bpfjctl, bpfjcmd and bpfjtest, and the development key
# `make signing-key` creates. The source tree itself is never written to --
# `make test` included, whose per-test mounts and temp directories live under
# /tmp and are removed as each test is reaped.
#
# BUILD is overridable, and a second configuration conventionally takes the
# build-* shape, as in `make BUILD=build-asan SANITIZE=address,undefined`. A
# tree built somewhere else entirely needs that path ignored on its own.
/build/
/build-*/
